    },
    {
      "id": "J__R6ybeBkpeLxkj6lj0V",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1138.5000938222652,
      "y": 439,
      "width": 588.5197143554688,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0b",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 242012909,
      "version": 968,
      "versionNonce": 333421507,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792849444665,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Wave: a group of thread blocks executing simulatenously.\nThe group of blocks running on the GPU at the same time.\n\nThe ratio of the total number of thread blocks in the grid\nto the number that can execute simultaneously is \nreferred to as the number of waves. \n\nWaves = Total blocks / blocks that fit at once, rounded UP\n(div_ceil, like the grid).\n\nBlocks that fit at once = SMs x blocks per SM (here,\nsimplified to 1 block per SM). In reality,\nan SM holds several blocks.\n\nA partly empty wave still costs a full wave of time:\nthe tail effect. \n\nBlocks per SM = the SM's limits (threads, blocks,\nregisters, shared memory) / what one block of \nthe kernel uses; the tightest of the 4 wins.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Wave: a group of thread blocks executing simulatenously.\nThe group of blocks running on the GPU at the same time.\n\nThe ratio of the total number of thread blocks in the grid\nto the number that can execute simultaneously is \nreferred to as the number of waves. \n\nWaves = Total blocks / blocks that fit at once, rounded UP\n(div_ceil, like the grid).\n\nBlocks that fit at once = SMs x blocks per SM (here,\nsimplified to 1 block per SM). In reality,\nan SM holds several blocks.\n\nA partly empty wave still costs a full wave of time:\nthe tail effect. \n\nBlocks per SM = the SM's limits (threads, blocks,\nregisters, shared memory) / what one block of \nthe kernel uses; the tightest of the 4 wins.\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ByD226o-GBSruu4rUtMFI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -87.6298828125,
      "y": 282,
      "width": 410.759765625,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0c",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 391607917,
      "version": 114,
      "versionNonce": 201030541,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792848752744,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In this example, the GPU has 2 SMs\nand each SM can hold one block at a time.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In this example, the GPU has 2 SMs\nand each SM can hold one block at a time.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
